Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||11-20-2001||09:18 PM||||I am no expert, but I did stay at a Holiday Inn last night  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P>I do own a book to try and help me install a turbo into my car (still thinking about it). It's called Maximum Boost, and Corky (the guy that wrote it) says that little turbo will give you some awesome 0-30 times, but after that it will be nothing more than an obstruction in the exhaust and pretty much a torch for the intake charge (Very fast compressor = highly compressed air = very hot = detonation).<P>I would think you need a turbo with an exhaust a/r of around .75. That's what I would choose. I bet that Sunbird is around .50 or so (just guessing), but it is a small turbo.||||reg||1
